So far in November 2026, **GVZ (GVZCLS) has averaged about 26.43.**

I pulled the daily FRED closes from November 1 to 24 and averaged them. FRED has 15 trading days so far, from November 2 to November 20. Nothing after November 20 has been published yet, so this is a month-to-date figure and will change.

- **Mean:** 26.43 (standard deviation 2.64)
- **Median:** 25.83
- **Range:** 24.11 (Nov 4) to 34.80 (Nov 20)

The month was calm until the last few days. GVZ stayed between about 24 and 26.5 through November 17, then climbed to 28.04, 28.70 and finally 34.80 on November 20. That one-day jump of about 6 points lifts the average noticeably: without November 20, the mean of the first 14 days would be about 25.83.

So the median, 25.83, better describes most of the month. If gold volatility stays near the latest level, the November average will keep rising as more data comes in.